>> title: Tortilla Española
>> category: Eggs
>> tags: eggs, potatoes, spanish, one-pot, skillet, tapas
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: tortilla de patatas, Spanish omelette, Spanish tortilla, potato omelette, tortilla de papas
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the turn happens once: flipped before the base has set it collapses onto the plate, left until firm all through it is dry
>> washing-up: the nonstick skillet, a bowl to beat the eggs in, a plate to turn it on
>> keeps: 3 days — meant to be eaten at room temperature, so the second day costs it almost nothing

>> step: The oil is poured off rather than strained and the potato is lifted straight into the beaten egg.
One pan, one bowl and a plate to turn it on.

>> step: fry gently 20 min, no colour
Fry @Yukon Gold potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; peeled, sliced thin), @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced thin) in @olive oil{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL) in a #nonstick skillet{} for ~fry{20%min}, moving them so they soften without browning.

>> step: beat, lift the potato in, stand 10 min
Beat @eggs{6}, @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in a bowl, lift @&(~1)fried potatoes{} into them with a slotted spoon, pour off all but a spoonful of the oil, and ~stand{10%min}.

>> step: set 8 min over low heat
Set @&(~1)potato and egg{} back in the pan over low heat for ~fry{8%min}, pulling the edge in as it firms.

>> step: turn out onto a plate, slide back, 4 min
Flip @&(~1)tortilla{} onto a plate, slide it back in raw side down, and ~fry{4%min}.

>> step: Cover the pan, take both in one grip and tip it over in one movement. Rest five minutes before cutting.
The turn is the whole trick and a plate does it.
